-- The other side of setWitnessNegatedComparisonBoundary's closure: a point
-- removed from the inside of an interval stays removed, so p(Right 0.0) is
-- impossible, while the interval's own closed bound -1.0 answers the density.
-- (An interior point is an event of its own: `x == 0.0` meeting its
-- complement is empty, set-witness/setWitnessContinuousEqualsTwice.)
main = draw v = Normal in if (v > -1.0) && not (v == 0.0) then right v else left ()
